<title>BELGIUM: BELGIAN NATL BANK SAYS HAS NOT SOLD ANY MORE GOLD.</title>
<headline>BELGIAN NATL BANK SAYS HAS NOT SOLD ANY MORE GOLD.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-12-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Belgium's central bank on Thursday dismissed a market rumour it may have sold more gold in recent days.</p>
<p>&quot;No we haven't,&quot; a spokesman for the bank told Reuters.</p>
<p>Rumours that either the Italian, Dutch, French or Belgian central banks were discreetly selling gold were cited by London traders on Thursday as one reason gold prices have been depressed in recent days.</p>
<p>Belgium has sold some 700 tonnes of its gold reserves since 1989. Recently it said it would use the proceeds to help cut its debt ahead of European economic and monetary union.</p>
<p>-- Nick Antonovics, Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6817, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
